--- Reads file and outputs it to stdout, then outputs it to tmp.tmt ---

This is "Hello Example" that should listen to `./00_hello.tmt`.

If _$"ERROR"_ = _$"FILE READ ERROR"_
Then
    Tell error `Could not read file $"Hello Example": $"ERROR MESSAGE"\n`.
    Quit _$"ERROR"_.
That's it.


Say the meaning of "Hello Example";

Tell `./tmp.tmt` the meaning of "Hello Example".

If _$"ERROR"_ = _$"FILE WRITE ERROR"_
Then
    Tell error `Could not write to file './tmp.tmt': `, the meaning of "ERROR MESSAGE", `\n`.
    Quit _$"ERROR"_.
That's it.
